//! Caravan appeal -- the reader who is told how a quarrel came out may answer
//! that telling, rather than read a door that only opens outward.
//!
//! `tidings.rye` carried the whole arc's finding back to the person it began
//! with: one byte into that reader's own box, naming whether the word they
//! objected to reads differently now or reads exactly as it read. That is the
//! first thing this arc ever sent outward, and it is right.
//!
//! **It is also the last word.** A reader told `t` -- your word stood -- has
//! read a season's answer to their own quarrel and has nowhere to put what they
//! think of it. They may accept it, they may press the case still, and either
//! way the plan hears nothing: every note above this rung travels one direction,
//! from the run to the reader, and the run never looks back.
//!
//! **The measurement is readers who answered how their quarrel came out and
//! whom no run ever read.** The rung below weighs what the arc finally reached
//! at the person it began with. This one weighs what that person reached back --
//! a reply written in their own hand into their own box, sitting there unread
//! while the plan reports itself finished.
//!
//! **An appeal is read where the reader wrote it, and recorded where an operator
//! reads.** The act is two halves and they face opposite ways: one byte the
//! reader writes into their own `.press` -- `a` for an outcome they accept, `p`
//! for a quarrel they press still -- and one byte the run writes into
//! `plan.appeal`, so an operator opening this plan reads whether the person who
//! raised the quarrel is content with how it came out.
//!
//! **A plea is quoted, and never composed.** No run of this plan ever writes a
//! reader's `.press`, exactly as no run writes their answer or their renewal.
//! A supervisor that could file a plea on a reader's behalf would be pressing an
//! objection it invented and then reading its own handwriting back as consent.
//!
//! **A plan publishes whether it reads back at all.** A record written
//! `appeal = .open` says: whoever was told how their quarrel came out may say
//! what they think of it, and be heard. `appeal = .closed` is where the rung
//! below leaves it -- the outcome sent, the reply unread, the record silent
//! about whether anybody accepted a word of it. The word sits at the plan beside
//! the tidings, since it instructs about who a record listens to rather than
//! about any one phase.
//!
//! **The rung earns four refusals, and each is about the reading back rather
//! than the quarrel it closes.** `AppealEarly` is the moment: a run reading a
//! plea where nobody was ever told is hearing a reply to a letter it never sent.
//! `AppealUnvoiced` is the hard half -- a plea recorded where the reader's own
//! hand wrote nothing is a supervisor filing an objection on their behalf and
//! calling it theirs. `AppealMiscounted` is the honesty of the count: every
//! reader this run told is heard again or left unheard, never both and never
//! neither. `AppealMisrecorded` is the record -- a published plea that disagrees
//! with the byte in the reader's own box tells every future operator the wrong
//! thing about a living person.
//!
//! **A plan the wire holds no quarrel about reads as the rung below.** With no
//! disagreement recorded, nobody is told, nobody is read back, no standing is
//! published, no amendment is posted, nothing is carried, nothing is heard,
//! nothing is escorted, nothing is asked, each line stands at the width it was
//! handed, and the door answers `unhand.admissible_held` pair for pair -- this
//! arc's standing generalization test, one tier further out.
//!
//! Usage:
//!   appeal            Run the self-test (default)
//!   appeal selftest   Same as default
//!   appeal dependent ...  Run as one supervised dependent (spawned by the run)

const std = @import("std");
const assert = std.debug.assert;
const print = std.debug.print;
const system = @import("system.rye");
const capabilities = @import("capabilities.rye");
const roster = @import("roster.rye");
const read = @import("read.rye");
const boot = @import("boot.rye");
const exercise = @import("exercise.rye");
const carry = @import("carry.rye");
const notify = @import("notify.rye");
const roundtrip = @import("roundtrip.rye");
const cycle = @import("cycle.rye");
const regions = @import("regions.rye");
pub const queue_store = @import("queue.rye");
pub const serve = @import("serve.rye");
const gap = @import("gap.rye");
const cohort = @import("cohort.rye");
const intent = @import("intent.rye");
const mask = @import("mask.rye");
const precede = @import("precede.rye");
const overtake = @import("overtake.rye");
const unhand = @import("unhand.rye");
const entrust = @import("entrust.rye");
const confer = @import("confer.rye");
pub const revoke_rung = @import("revoke.rye");
const reclaim_rung = @import("reclaim.rye");
const abandon_rung = @import("abandon.rye");
const bearing_rung = @import("bear.rye");
const couriering_rung = @import("courier.rye");
